# D15 — DictionaryNodeRegistry exact-key interning.
# Depicts: how dictionary nodes (which lack inherent ids) get stable u32 ids via a compact exact
# path-step key, plus the Arc<RwLock> concurrency boundary.
direction: right

title: |md
  # D15 · DictionaryNodeRegistry — stable node ids by exact path-step key
| { near: top-center }

trie: "Dictionary trie traversal\n(parent node, edge label)" { style.fill: "#D5F5E3"; style.stroke: "#34495E" }
key: "DictionaryNodeKey::child(parent_id, edge_label)\n(parent << 21) | char" { style.fill: "#EAECEE"; style.stroke: "#34495E" }

registry: "DictionaryNodeRegistry  (Arc<RwLock<…>>)" {
  style.fill: "#D6EAF8"; style.stroke: "#34495E"
  fwd: "node_to_id:\nFxHashMap<DictionaryNodeKey, u32>" { style.fill: "#FFFFFF"; style.stroke: "#34495E" }
  rev: "id_to_node:\nVec<Node>" { style.fill: "#FFFFFF"; style.stroke: "#34495E" }
}

id: "stable u32 node id\n(used in StateId = d·M + a)" { style.fill: "#D6EAF8"; style.stroke: "#34495E" }

trie -> key -> registry.fwd: "intern" { style.stroke: "#2ECC71" }
registry.fwd -> id { style.stroke: "#2ECC71" }
id -> registry.rev: "id_to_node[id]" { style.stroke: "#E67E22"; style.stroke-dash: 3 }

invariant: |md
  **Exactness invariant:** child keys pack `u32 parent_id` plus the 21-bit Unicode scalar value of
  `edge_label`; `u64::MAX` is reserved for the root. `FxHashMap` may collide internally, but equality
  checks prevent node aliasing. Read/write access is guarded by `RwLock`; crate-local helpers recover
  poisoned guards with `PoisonError::into_inner()`.
| { near: bottom-center; style.fill: "#E8F8F5"; style.stroke: "#16A085" }
